# t.z -- a user unit named `t`, the name of the system library's most common
# generic parameter. A dotted type-ref asked whether its qualifier named a unit
# before asking whether its member was a marker, so with this unit loaded
# OptionViewVal's `some: t.borrow` read as a type `borrow` in it: every program
# failed in system.z (E0023 "Unknown type 'borrow'"), and an iterator's item
# typed as `borrow`. A marker is a reserved word and so no unit's member;
# `X.borrow` is the marker form whatever X names.
double: function {x: u64} out u64 is {
    return x * 2
}

# a unit type spelled through the unit, marked: `t.Box.view` is the type `Box`
# of this unit, viewed
Box: record {
    n: u64
}
